<title>DENMARK: Danish Danisco appoints new chief exec.</title>
<headline>Danish Danisco appoints new chief exec.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish food and drinks group Danisco A/S on Tuesday appointed Alf Duch-Pedersen as new chief executive to succeed outgoing Palle Marcus effective April 1, 1997.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Marcus had decided to take up his contractual option to retire on his 60th birthday and planned to assume a number of posts on other company boards.</p>
<p>Duch-Pedersen, 50, takes over his new Danisco CEO post after five years as president and chief executive of Denmark's leading Tryg-Baltica insurance group.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
